 "rules": [
  "A Winter Permit is needed for ALL backcountry access, Unrestricted Areas too. Carry it with government photo ID; digital is fine. Fine up to $25,000.",
  "Annual permit: apply online, allow a week or more; needed for huts and overnights. Daily permit: only at Summit Station on the day, after the quiz.",
  "A national park pass for everyone, and the printed Winter Parking Permit on the dashboard (plate must match).",
  "Winter Restricted Areas open or stay closed each day for artillery fire: status posted about 7:30 am. Restricted parking closes at midnight.",
  "Winter Prohibited Areas are closed all winter: skier avalanches could reach the highway, or the snow is kept for forecasting.",
  "No camping or overnight use in a Winter Restricted Area. No sleeping in vehicles. No drones.",
  "Keep at least 16 m from the CP railway and use the designated access routes. No stopping in signed avalanche areas on the highway.",
  "If you come back to a card on your windshield, avalanche control started: wait with your car until Parks Canada says the highway is open."
